  "tier": "told-once",
  "plain": "The researcher Scott Ramsey says he and his colleagues traced nine of the unnamed scientists behind a book called Behind the Flying Saucers, known in the book as \"Dr. G,\" to the circle of Vannevar Bush. Bush was the engineer who ran the Office of Scientific Research and Development, the US government's wartime science agency in the 1940s. Ramsey says they went \"down each division\" of Bush's group and recognised name after name, among them Richard C. Tolman, Eugene McDermott and Cecil Howard Green, which he takes as a sign that the book's sources were real wartime insiders."
}
